@startuml
title Event feed: resume, stream, fall back
participant "SwiftUI feed" as UI
participant "Core FeedState" as Core
participant "Host helper `feed`" as H
database "Session file / agy .db" as F
UI -> Core: open(session, saved cursor)
Core -> H: exec `feed --session S --since inode:offset` (one channel)
H -> F: stat (inode, size) then read [offset, size) up to last newline
H --> Core: hello {proto:1}
alt cursor valid
  H --> Core: append/update events (batch of what was missed)
else file replaced, shorter or unknown cursor
  H --> Core: reset {last N turns, new cursor}
end
loop while the connection lives
  F -> H: new bytes / changed steps
  H --> Core: append | update (coalesced, <= 256 KB each)
  H --> Core: live {status, draft, prompt} only when changed
  Core -> UI: change set (added ids, updated ids)
  UI -> UI: insert / replace rows by id
end
UI -> Core: app goes to background
Core -> H: channel closed (helper exits on write error or EOF)
note over Core: cursor kept; foreground repeats `open`
alt helper missing or proto mismatch
  Core -> Core: screen path (today's behaviour)
end
@enduml
